	Introduction, Preface
    
	Finaly I've rewritten this 6 months old documentation and given
	it a new look that should be far more easier to read and get some
	hints from. This is revision V1.05 and you might have to take a
	closer look at some upgraded fascillities that is not compatible
	with V1.04 & V1.03, but here we go from the begining so hang on ..

	Account Editor (Short name AccED) is a so called ARexx Door for
	the /X 2.35+ package and will interfer as an AIM (Arexx Interface
        Module). If you use this door you can make the security on your
	board even higher with the high security features of this door.

	The source is not compiled and should be rather easy for an ARexx
	programmer to take a look at, which you also should do if you
	wan't to be sure there is no backdoors provided with the source
	from one in the row of people who got it before you. To be sure
	wether there is a backdoor or not you should call my board INSANiTY
	which is the official distrubtion site for my doors and my /X
	echo mail package which is available for a nominal fee. I'm right
	now doing a major update on that program so it can aproximatly
	be delivered first at May. ßeta versions will be available sooner.

  /\  __________________/\/\_________________/\___________ _  _  _   _    _
 /  \/
	What will AccED do for you?

	Account Ed is designed with high security in mind and I think my
	door is the first one that can lock out a user at a specific time
	period, ie between 24.00 and 08.00 in the morning if you think
	that no one should access the account editor then.

	It also checks if a person got the right name from a list of
	persons alloved to use the account editor. This works in the same
	way as Maltese Falcons Remote Shell and Sysop Download utils.

	Every entry in the user data that someone who is in Account ED
	look at will be reported and logged in a speciall Account ED log
	file. It will also add comments if someone read or wrote an account
	and if you print an account. Yes, you could actually print an account
	to your printer using the printer settings from your Amiga DOS.
	This feature is really my favorite, if you are going to delete an
	user you could easily print the users account before selecting
	delete and store it somewhere for no good but anyway ..

	You can lock certain functions in the account editor for your
	cosysops so they only could use the 6 pre defined presets, no
	I'm joking .. 6 presets, NO! the 9 pre defined presets with a
	comment which you can write so the cosysop knows what each preset
	stands for and for which users they are meant. Nice ehh!?

	Like the MCP (Master Control Program) by Bryce, you can give and
	take access for a conference for all your users, so if you close
	a conference you easily can delete all users access to it or if
	you simple have started a new area. But.. wouldn't it be nice to
	go a litle bit further and include one more nice feature into that
	powerfull command? Yes! You can define between which two access
	levels a user must be so you could give/take access from users who
	only has got the security level 30 to 40 ie.

	As the need to check for a user that you by mistake has given a too
	high security level even grows stronger the more hackers there
	are around I've included the feature to get a list of all users
	between to certain security levels so you could use 200 to 255 or
	if you simple wan't a whole userlist you type 1 to 255 ..
	This section of Account ED also includes the possibility to get
	a list of all users who has got access to a certain conference for
	instance your groups member conference 5!

	Back to the main account editor there are some major line ups if
	you compare to the built in editor. First of all the design is
	made to be easy to overview and fast to get some particular
	information about one user. The built in one was so messy that I
	had a hard time to understand my own account with the download /
	upload cps and location put like a joke on the screen. This is
	should be easy to read and each function has got new letters
	becouse the old ones was worn out and not well placed. I hope
	you'll soon learn the new keys!

	The help page inside the account editor is for easy access to
	the most common functions inside the editor. You simple press
	a key and you can view it at the same time as the account is on
	the same page so you easily could compare and so on. If you
	have used my Questionary Door called Quest (last version V1.09)
	this program is fully compatible with Quest. Anytime when you
	are reading a persons account you could press a key and get that
	users questionary on your screen. Very usefull if you upgrade
	first time users.. I think you remeber yourself loading a text-
	editor with your Answers file and trying to upgrade that poor
	users account, but how did your cosysops manage!? I guess that
	they didn't and the security with new users failed on your board!

	Ever wanted a function that writes a letter very fast to your
	users and saying that they should upload and shows the users
	stats with uploaded/download bytes & file, calls and message?
	Well it's built in into Account ED!

	Another thing that can make you nervs popp up is then you have
	to delete old recieved messages from users who has not choosen
	delete then they've replied letters and all those EALL messages
	that you new users hate.. Account ED has a built in function
	which scanns your msgbase and deletes old mail and asks what
	you want to do with the EALL messages!!

	You can give a speciall access level for viewing the passwords
	of all acounts, if you do not have this security level Account ED
	will prompt Not Displayed as a password. You can choose if the
	password default should be shown to the ones with the security
	level or they have to press a special key combination for the
	password to appear. Usefull if you have some friends beside you!

	What about security for your groups conference then? Well as this
	program has been around a while I've thought of that too, so you
	could specify a conference to which no one could give access!
	This means that your cosysop not can give himself access to your
	groups member area!!

	Ok I see that you are beginning to understand why I developed
	this new account editor, so I will now give you only one more
	reason to use it. If you sometimes have an upload competion on
	your board you know how anyoing it is to give that poor winner
	his rewareded upload credits, it usually means that you have
	to run down the stairs to get a pocket calculator and then
	enter his new upload bytes. But you could stop doing that
	already today if you use this account editor with built in
	calculator which can add and sub from a users account. You just
	choose the field you wan't to change and use the upper case of
	the letter instead and you will be asked if you wan't to sub or
	add and how many bytes. This works for all fields that has got
	to do with upload, download and limits.

	Oh, sorry I forgot to tell you one thing. In the /X account editor
	when you choose ie to change the users uploaded creds it clears
	that field and you have to try to remember what there was standing.
	My account editor will not remove anything that you don't write
	over and when you move the cursor with the backspace key it won't
	remove any letters from the screen, but just in memory so you
	easily could remeber what was standing there before and you then
	can write over it!

	These is more features than many doors together can't even handle!
	So you'd better take a closer look or you'll regret it!

