	Instalation ..

	Snap the following row to your BBS:Commands/BBS.Cmd file:

	*1        Rm230Doors:Arexx/Account/AccEd.rexx

	This will let all users with security level 230 and higher access
	the account editor if their names are in the allowed user list.

	When you have managed to do that it would be time to move the
	Account ED package to your Doors:Arexx/ path, which is the path
	all my doors requires so you better not put it elsewhere.

	Previous user must note that there should be 3 new directories inside
	the Account/ direcotry called: QuestApp, QuestDel and QuestQst.
	if you are previous running Quest and has got it in the
	Doors:Arexx/Quest/ dir you should move your questions from the answers
	dir to the QuestApp dir in the Account directory. Otherwise Account ED
	can't get the questionaries! (More info in the Quest doc file)

	After doing that you should edit the AccEd.Presets file which
	shall contain your personal presets and comments. I will only
	give a brief explenation on how that file works, you have to
	find out the rest by yourself!

	The 7 present at the left top edge is the numbers of presets you
	are going to have. To add one for instance add the number to 8
	and enter the new values under the 7:th preset. 2359 and 0730 is the
	time period when no one has got access to Account ED. The names
	located under the presets is all users who are allowed to use
	the account editor.

	  Comment         SecL  RaT Rat Aut  Bytelimit ConfAccess  TimeLim  Computers
	7--------------------------------------------------------------1.05-------------------
Preset1	| Lamer          | 5   | 1 | 2 | 1 | 100000   | X________ | 1200  | Amiga 500        |
Preset2 | PD User        | 20  | 1 | 3 | 2 | 500000   | X_X__X_X_ | 3600  | Amiga 500+       |
Preset3 | Elite User     | 30  | 1 | 3 | 4 | 2500000  | X_XX_X_X_ | 3600  | Amiga 600        |
Preset4	| Elite Trader   | 40  | 1 | 3 | 7 | 5000000  | X_X__XXX_ | 4800  | Amiga 1000       |
Preset5	| Virtual Member | 50  | 1 | 0 | 4 | 10000000 | X_XXXX_X_ | 7200  | Amiga 1200       |
Preset6	| Virtual Member | 50  | 1 | 0 | 7 | 10000000 | X_X_XXXX_ | 7200  | Amiga 2000       |
Preset7	| Proud CoSysop  | 230 | 0 | 0 | 7 | 10000000 | X_XX_XXXX | 14400 | Amiga 3000       |
Preset8	|                |     |   |   |   |          |           |       | Amiga 4000       |
Preset9	|                |     |   |   |   |          |           |       | PC Com 286       |
	2359-----------------------------------------------------------0730 PC Com 386       |
	| Delusion Sauna Fox D-Zire                                       | PC Com 486       |
	------------------------------------------------------------------- PC Com 586       |
	| UserData Path    | BBS:User.Data      | Enable Seclevel  |  255 | Atari 1040       |
	| UserKeys Path    | BBS:User.Keys      | ChangeAcc Seclev |  255 | Other            |
	| Write Note Path  | BBS:Conf-7         | MsgBaseClean Sec |  255 |                  |
	| AccED Password   | Transworld         | See Users Pass   |  255 |                  |
	| DeleteQuest Pass | Bobolink           | Show Users Pass  |  Off |                  |
	| Recieve App Mail | Delusion           | Print Account    |   On |                  |
	| AccountED Colour | [0m               | Search New Users |  300 |                  |
	| Log Status AccED | 4                  | Members Conf     |    5 |                  |
	| Reserved Nothing |                    | Kickout After X  |    5 |------------------|
	| Reserved Nothing |                    | Questionary      |    4 | AccountED © 1993 |
	| AutoAccess Quest | No                 | MustEnter No Ret |  Yes | Delusion of VTL! |
	--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

	In previous preset files the computer list was in this form:
	Amiga 500¬Amiga 1000¬ and so on, now it should stand in descending
	order in the column which says computers.

	Under the names with the persons who has got access to Account
	(Delusion Sauna Fox D-Zire) is all the configuration datas for both
	Quest and Account ED, all values who has got to do with Quest is
	explained separately in the Quest Doc so here comes the explanations:

	UserData Path	- The path on you harddrive where your userdata is

	UserData Keys	- The path on you harddrive where your userkeys is

	Write Note Path - This is the path to the conference where you wan't
			  the warning notes made in Account ED to come
			  This should be a path to one of your 9 conferences

	AccED Password	- If you wan't to enter a password to use Account ED
			  you should enter a password here, if this line
			  is empty Account Ed wont ask you for a password

	DeleteQuestPass - This is the password a user has to enter if he
			  want's to delete a users questionary (application)

	AccountEdColour - This is the colour in which all data in the AccED
			  will be displayed in

	Log Status AccEd- Maybe you don't wan't to log every action taken in
			  Account ED, then you should change the Log variabel.
			  Here is what the different numbers means:

			  1, Log only when an account is read
			  2, Log only when an account is saved
			  3, Log both read and save
			  4, Log both read and save, but not then sysop does it!
			  0, Log nothing

	Enable Seclevel	- This is the security level a user has got to have to
			  change anything in a users account than the name,
			  location and autorejoin conference. A user with
			  lower status than the enable status can however use
			  the nine presets, which is the meaning that the user
			  should use instead. I recomend that you lower your
			  cosysops security level to 230 and keep yours at 255.
			  They can not logon your password becouse a user can
			  not look at the slot number 1 and they can not give
			  anyone higher security level than they self got, so
			  a cosysop with 230 can not give himself security
			  level 255 and play sysop which is the case with the
			  built in account editor!

	ChangeAcc Seclev- This is the access level a user has got to have if
			  he want's to give or take access from all users for
			  a certain conference.	I explained that command in
			  the features so read more about it there!

	MsgBaseClean Sec- The access level required to use the built in
			  message base cleaner, to delete old recieved mail

	See Users Pass	- If you do not have this access level or higher you
			  won't be able	to se different users passwords when
			  using the account editor. Have you sometime asked
			  yourself the question, why should my cosysop se
			  other users passwords, then he just should upgrade
			  users accounts!?

	Show Users Pass - This option works like this.. If a user has got the
			  requested security level entered at SeePass the user
			  will then be able to se another users password, but
			  if this option is turned Off your user has to	push
			  Shift+C to see the password and edit it. If he
			  doesn't there	will only stand Not Displayed. If you
			  have choosed to let your cosysops view the users
			  passwords, but don't wan't them to see them by
			  defualt you should choose Off, if you always wan't
			  to see the password you should choose On and the
			  passwords will be displayed if you have SeePass
			  security level.

	Print Account	- If you do not own a printer you should deffinently
			  chose Off as a printer option, or if you don't wan't
			  anyone to print an account.

	Search New Users- This one is made to increase the speed when searching
			  for new users. If you know that you will never get a
			  new user with the slot number under 300, then choose
			  300 and the Account Editor will start to search for
			  new users beginning at the slot number 300!

	Members Conf	- As my board is Virtual European HeadQuarter and main
			  board for all our comming productions and so on in
			  our special member area, I found it very anoying
			  with cosysops giving them selves access to that
			  conference just of curiosity. That problem has now
			  been eliminated with this feature letting the sysop
			  specify a conference where no one can give themselves
			  access too. The only way to give a user access to
			  conference is to use the built in /X editor on the F6
			  key when someone is currently online!

	This is how it could look. Do not snap this one, use the supplied
	one in this archive called AccEd.Presets. Please note that everything
	is position dependant, all configuration parameters must stand between
	a | and a | so it could look like this |         BBS:User.Data | or
	| BBS:User.Data.          | it doesn't matter.

	If you have any questions concerning this rather complicated config
	file, don't be afraid to call my board and ask!

	You should now be finished with the instalation.

